  "body": "**What happens:** a tool has no number of its own. The post's `T..`/`H..` is the tool's 1-based position in the document's tool list (`posting.rs`, `tool_ranks`). A document whose only tool is the user's T31 end mill (named \"Tool31 Lakeshore Carbide 360014X\") posts `T1 M6` / `G43 H1`.\n\n**Why it matters:** on a machine with a tool changer and a tool table, the program must call the controller's own number. With a Tormach ATC and electronic tool setter (#131), `T1 M6` loads whatever tool sits in pocket/number 1 and `G43 H1` applies T1's measured length. That's the wrong tool and the wrong length, with nothing in CamCraft to show it. It's the same on any control with a tool table.\n\n**Expected:** each tool in the library carries a tool number (and optionally a separate length-offset number H and diameter number D, defaulting to the tool number). The number is:\n- editable in the tool editor;\n- saved in the project and the tool library;\n- used by the post for `T`/`H` (and `D`).\n\nTwo tools with the same number refuse at post, by name. Documents without numbers keep today's list-order numbering, so existing goldens don't move.\n\n**Workaround today:** keep the document's tool order the same as the controller's numbering, or edit `T`/`H` in the posted file.\n\nSuggested labels (the filer can't set labels): `enhancement`, `P1`, `area:post`, `area:ui`, `source:agent`.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
